      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While empathy is crucial, traditional authoritative parenting offers a necessary balance by establishing consistent boundaries and natural consequences that foster true self-discipline. Unlike gentle parenting's heavy reliance on negotiation, this approach teaches children that rules exist for their own benefit, not just to please an authority. Consequently, it builds the resilience and emotional maturity required to navigate life's inevitable challenges without constant parental intervention. Embracing this structure empowers children to become independently responsible adults rather than perpetual learners dependent on external reassurance.",
